---
import PolicyLayout from "../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro";
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | ATL TV Mount"
  description="Privacy Policy for ATL TV Mount, operated by Northline Mounting Services LLC."
>
  <p class="policy-kicker">Legal</p>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="policy-updated">Last updated: September 22, 2026</p>

  <div class="policy-content">
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>ATL TV Mount, operated by Northline Mounting Services LLC</strong>
      (“ATL TV Mount,” “Northline,” “we,” “us,” or “our”) collects, uses, and protects information when you
      visit our website, request an estimate, book a service, communicate with us, or receive services from us.
    </p>

    <h2>Information We Collect</h2>

    <p>Depending on how you interact with us, we may collect:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Name</li>
      <li>Phone number</li>
      <li>Email address</li>
      <li>Service address</li>
      <li>Appointment and scheduling information</li>
      <li>Information about your TV, mounting location, wall type, equipment, and requested services</li>
      <li>Photographs or other files you send to us</li>
      <li>SMS, MMS, email, and other communications with us</li>
      <li>Payment-related information processed through our payment providers</li>
      <li>
        Website usage and technical information, such as browser type, device information, pages viewed,
        referral information, and interactions with the website
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How We Use Information</h2>

    <p>We may use information to:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Respond to inquiries</li>
      <li>Prepare estimates and pricing</li>
      <li>Schedule and manage appointments</li>
      <li>Provide TV mounting and related services</li>
      <li>Communicate about estimates, appointments, arrival times, and completed services</li>
      <li>Respond to photographs or installation information submitted by customers</li>
      <li>Process payments</li>
      <li>Maintain business and transaction records</li>
      <li>Improve our website, services, pricing, and customer experience</li>
      <li>Measure website and advertising performance</li>
      <li>Protect our website, customers, and business from misuse, fraud, or security threats</li>
      <li>Comply with applicable legal obligations</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>SMS and MMS Communications</h2>

    <p>
      ATL TV Mount uses SMS and MMS for <strong>customer-initiated conversations and service-related communications only</strong>.
    </p>

    <p>Messages may include:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Responses to customer questions</li>
      <li>Estimates and service discussions</li>
      <li>Appointment confirmations</li>
      <li>Appointment reminders</li>
      <li>Scheduling or arrival updates</li>
      <li>Service-related follow-ups</li>
      <li>Responses regarding photographs or installation details</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      <strong>
        We do not use SMS or MMS for advertising campaigns, promotional messages, newsletters,
        mass marketing, or unsolicited outreach.
      </strong>
    </p>

    <p>
      Customers may receive messages after initiating a text conversation with us or after providing
      appropriate consent through an eligible website form.
    </p>

    <p>Message frequency varies.</p>

    <p>Message and data rates may apply.</p>

    <p>
      Reply <strong>STOP</strong> to opt out of SMS/MMS messages. Reply <strong>HELP</strong> for assistance
      or contact us at <a href="mailto:info@atltvmount.com">info@atltvmount.com</a>.
    </p>

    <p>Consent to receive SMS/MMS messages is not a condition of purchasing our services.</p>

    <h2>Mobile Information and SMS Consent</h2>

    <p>
      No mobile information will be shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes.
      SMS opt-in data, mobile phone numbers, and messaging consent will not be sold, rented, or shared with
      third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes.
    </p>

    <p>
      Service providers acting on our behalf may process this information only as reasonably necessary
      to provide communications and related operational services.
    </p>

    <h2>Photographs of Completed Work</h2>

    <p>
      We may photograph completed TV mounting and installation work for documentation, portfolio,
      website, social media, Google Business Profile, advertising, and other marketing purposes.
    </p>

    <p>Customers may request that their installation <strong>not be photographed</strong>.</p>

    <p>
      We do not intentionally publish customer names, street addresses, personal documents, people,
      or other clearly identifying personal information in installation photographs without separate permission.
    </p>

    <p>
      If you do not want photographs taken of your completed installation, please notify us before
      or during the service appointment.
    </p>

    <p>
      If a photograph of your installation has already been published and you would like us to review
      a removal request, contact us at
      <a href="mailto:info@atltvmount.com">info@atltvmount.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Payments</h2>

    <p>Payment is generally collected after the requested work has been completed.</p>

    <p>We may accept:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Major credit or debit cards processed through Square</li>
      <li>Zelle</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      We do not store full payment card numbers. Card payments are processed by Square.
      Zelle payments are processed through participating financial institutions.
    </p>

    <h2>Service Providers and Third-Party Platforms</h2>

    <p>
      We may use third-party service providers to operate our website and business, including services for:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>Website hosting and infrastructure, including Cloudflare</li>
      <li>Website analytics through Google Analytics</li>
      <li>Advertising measurement through Google Ads</li>
      <li>Tag and analytics management through Google Tag Manager</li>
      <li>Scheduling and calendar functionality through Google Calendar</li>
      <li>SMS/MMS communications through Twilio</li>
      <li>Payment processing through Square</li>
      <li>Electronic payments through Zelle</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      These providers may process information as necessary to perform services on our behalf
      and may also operate under their own privacy policies and terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and Analytics Technologies</h2>

    <p>
      Our website may use cookies, local storage, tags, pixels, and similar technologies for essential
      website functionality, security, analytics, performance measurement, and advertising measurement.
    </p>

    <p>
      We use services such as Google Analytics, Google Ads, Google Tag Manager, and Cloudflare
      that may use these technologies.
    </p>

    <p>
      Google may process information collected through our use of Google services as described in
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services
      </a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      You may also manage certain Google advertising preferences through
      <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      Additional information about technologies used on this website and available controls
      is provided in our <a href="/cookies">Cookies Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Sharing of Information</h2>

    <p>We do not sell personal information.</p>

    <p>
      We may disclose information to service providers that help us operate our business,
      but only as reasonably necessary for them to perform those services.
    </p>

    <p>We may also disclose information when reasonably necessary to:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Comply with applicable laws or legal requests</li>
      <li>Protect our legal rights</li>
      <li>Prevent fraud or misuse</li>
      <li>Protect customers, employees, service providers, or the public</li>
      <li>Enforce our agreements</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      The disclosures described above do not permit the sale or sharing of SMS opt-in data,
      mobile phone numbers, or messaging consent for marketing or promotional purposes.
      Such information may be processed by service providers acting on our behalf only as necessary
      to provide communications and related operational services.
    </p>

    <h2>Data Retention</h2>

    <p>
      We retain information for as long as reasonably necessary to provide requested services,
      maintain business and accounting records, manage customer relationships, resolve disputes,
      enforce agreements, prevent fraud or abuse, and meet applicable legal requirements.
    </p>

    <p>Different types of information may be retained for different periods.</p>

    <h2>Data Security</h2>

    <p>
      We use reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational measures designed to protect
      personal information. However, no website, communication method, database, or electronic
      storage system can be guaranteed to be completely secure.
    </p>

    <h2>Your Choices</h2>

    <p>
      You may contact us at
      <a href="mailto:info@atltvmount.com">info@atltvmount.com</a>
      to request access to, correction of, or deletion of personal information we maintain about you,
      subject to applicable law and legitimate business, accounting, security, and legal retention requirements.
    </p>

    <p>
      For SMS/MMS, reply <strong>STOP</strong> to opt out of text messages and
      <strong>HELP</strong> for assistance.
    </p>

    <p>You may also request that we do not photograph your completed installation.</p>

    <h2>Children’s Privacy</h2>

    <p>
      Our website and services are not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly
      collect personal information from children under 13.
    </p>

    <h2>External Websites and Services</h2>

    <p>
      Our website may contain links to or integrations with third-party websites and services.
      We are not responsible for the privacy practices of independent third parties.
      Their services are governed by their own privacy policies and terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>

    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The current version will be posted
      on this page and the “Last updated” date will be revised when appropriate.
    </p>

